# Phase 17 — Admin/query facade

- Started this execution on `phase/18-phase-17-admin-query` at `0a6402c1` with a clean worktree. Java source inspection used pinned commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`; the external Java checkout and its unrelated untracked file were left untouched.
- Implemented `Producer::create_topic` and `create_topic_with_sys_flag`: validate the namespaced topic, query the supplied route key, sort Brokers by Java UTF-16 broker-name order, target master addresses with the live VIP setting, retry each Broker five times, and accept partial success if any Broker creates the topic. The public producer facade's Java 5.5.1 wrapper discards its attributes argument, so the wire `attributes` field remains empty; namespace applies to the new topic while the key is passed through unchanged. The admin timeout is Java's 6000ms default.
- Added loopback tests for NameServer routing, topic namespace/header, Broker sorting, five retry attempts, partial success, last broker-error propagation, and validation before RPC. The first run exposed fixed group/client IDs colliding through the shared runtime manager; tests now allocate unique IDs. No live Broker was used.
- Verification: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-producer --locked` passed (92 unit tests, 4 admin tests, all other integration tests and doctests); `cargo fmt --all -- --check` passed; `cargo clippy -p rocketmq-classic-producer --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` passed. `git diff --check` passed.
- Phase 17 remains open: other MQAdmin methods, query fan-out, consumer facade exposure and client administrative processors are not complete. No plan file was modified.
- Continued Phase 17 on 2026-10-13 02:32 UTC. Rechecked the pinned Java source by reading commit `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` directly; the external checkout remains on that commit with only the previously known unrelated untracked Broker test file.
- Added `docs/compatibility/PHASE_17_ADMIN_MATRIX.md` as the P17-01 audit artifact. It distinguishes producer-only topic creation and queue APIs, Pull-only offset/queue methods, low-level single-Broker query/view RPCs, absent facade wrappers, and the four inbound administrative request codes which currently resolve to unsupported handlers. It records P17-V01/V03/U01 as local open evidence and keeps P17-V02 in Phase 19.
- Documentation-only verification: `git diff --check` passed. No tests were run for this documentation-only change. Phase 17 and Phase 18 remain open.
